      "title": "Changing rooms, clothes storage and lockers",
      "summary": "Changing rooms serve employees who wear working clothes and cannot reasonably change elsewhere. They should lie on the direct route between the site entrance and work area. Separate washing and changing rooms should be easily accessible to each other, with room for unobstructed changing by simultaneous users. If changing rooms are not required, provide clothes storage for each employee. Changing rooms must be separate for men and women and secure against draughts and outside view. Provide seating, lockers, waste bins and mirrors; a shoe-cleaning machine may also be appropriate.",
